==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|la|en}} {{m|la|praetermitto}}.

===Verb===
{{en-verb|pretermits|pretermitting|pretermitted}}

# To intentionally [[disregard]] something, allow it to go [[unnoticed]], or change the subject in response to someone's comment; to [[omit]] or fail to carry out something; to prematurely [[terminate]] or [[interrupt]] something.
#* The liberty of a subject lieth, therefore, only in those things which, in regulating their actions, the sovereign hath '''praetermitted''' (such as is the liberty to buy, and sell, and otherwise contract with one another; to choose their own abode, their own diet, their own trade of life, and institute their children as they themselves think fit; and the like). - Thomas Hobbes, ''Leviathan'', ch 21 section 6
#: {{rfquotek|Francis Bacon}}

